{%- comment -%}
  Composes the Mionas form snippets -- mionas-form / mionas-form-field / mionas-form-label /
  mionas-text-field / mionas-form-error, mirroring ../design-system/src/react/ -- around a single
  {% form 'contact' %}.

  Why this forks rather than reskinning blocks/contact-form.liquid: the native block hard-codes
  name+email onto one flex row, renders every label `visually-hidden` with text from
  blocks.contact_form.* locale keys, and includes a phone field this design does not have. It
  exposes no child field blocks, so a CSS bridge can restack and restyle it but cannot produce
  visible per-field labels carrying the design's own wording. See
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-25-contacto-page-design.md.

  THIS BLOCK OWNS ONLY THE FIELDS, THE SUBMIT BUTTON, AND THE FORM'S OWN VALIDATION/SUCCESS STATE --
  nothing else. No card, no heading, no WhatsApp CTA, no divider. blocks/mionas-email-signup.liquid
  follows the identical rule for its one field; read that file's header comment too, the two should
  never drift apart on this point. Every one of those excluded things is composable in the page
  template instead: a Mionas: Card wraps this block (and whatever siblings a page wants -- a
  Mionas: Text heading, a Mionas: Button CTA, another Mionas: Text as a lead-in line) when a carded
  look is wanted; a bare page with no card wrapper is equally valid. See
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-12-contacto-page-design.md.

  Two earlier versions of this file existed before landing here -- one where the block drew its own
  card around everything including a heading/WhatsApp button/divider it also owned, and one where it
  drew a narrower card around just the fields (matching an earlier reading of
  blocks/mionas-email-signup.liquid). Both put card ownership inside a form block; asked directly,
  the answer is that NEITHER a contact form nor an email signup should own a card at all -- the card
  is composition, not a form concern, and belongs in the template next to whatever the card is
  wrapping. Do not reintroduce a `.mionas-contact-form__card` (or any surface: background/border/
  radius/shadow) here.

  FIELD NAMING IS LOAD-BEARING. Per Shopify's own contact-form docs
  (shopify.dev/docs/storefronts/themes/customer-engagement/add-contact-form), contact[first_name],
  contact[last_name], contact[email], contact[phone], contact[body] and contact[order_number] are
  all natively recognised names -- do not rename any of these six. Keep the field names exactly
  contact[first_name], contact[last_name], contact[email] and contact[body] below.

  contact[request_type] is a CUSTOM field, not one of the six recognised names above -- Shopify
  titleizes a custom field's identifier into its label in the merchant notification email (its own
  docs use "request_type" -> "Request type" as the worked example for exactly this dropdown case),
  so it still reads cleanly, just as its own labelled line rather than folding into a native field.
  Renaming it to one of the six recognised names above would silently overwrite that field instead
  of adding a new one -- don't do that.

  Known platform limitation, same as blocks/corporate-quote-form.liquid: Shopify's `form` object
  only echoes back name, email, phone and body, so nothing custom repopulates after a validation
  error. Do not work around it.

  CLIENT-SIDE ERRORS ARE JS-DRIVEN ON PURPOSE. `validate: true` on the mionas-form render below
  loads assets/mionas-form-validation.js, which sets `novalidate` on the form FROM JAVASCRIPT and
  writes the same field/label classes and message paragraph the server-side `error` param produces,
  so the two error states are indistinguishable. Because novalidate is set from JS rather than in
  the form tag, a visitor without JavaScript keeps the browser's native validation. Do not move it
  into Liquid. type="email" on its own lets "marc@gmail" and "a@b" through, so
  snippets/mionas-text-field.liquid adds a stricter default `pattern` to every email field -- the
  regex and its reasoning live there. Shopify's own check is still the backstop and renders through
  the same markup.

  Only email is required, which is why the name and message labels carry the design system's
  " (optional)" suffix. That is FormLabel.tsx's own behaviour for a non-required field, not a
  styling accident.

  The submit button is NOT wrapped in snippets/mionas-form-actions.liquid. FormActions is a row with
  a start inset, meant for a button and a link side by side; this form has one full-width button,
  and the inset would leave it flush right but indented left. It IS still rendered by this block
  (unlike the card/heading/CTA above) because it must sit inside the <form> element to submit it --
  that is an HTML requirement, not a styling choice, so it cannot become a separate sibling block the
  way the card/heading/CTA could.

  The `note` param passed to snippets/mionas-submit-button.liquid below is that snippet's OWN note
  slot, not a duplicate paragraph -- do not re-add a bespoke `.mionas-contact-form__note` element.

  FIELD GAP IS A SETTING, NOT A HARDCODED VALUE. Both this block and mionas-email-signup expose a
  `field_gap` range, forwarded to snippets/mionas-form.liquid's `gap` param. Default matches
  Form.tsx's own `<Box gap="lg">` (--space-lg / 24px) so an untouched instance looks identical to
  before this setting existed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings
  assign form_id = block.id | prepend: 'MionasContactForm-'

  # Same layout-classes/width-custom-property pattern as blocks/mionas-email-signup.liquid, so the
  # two form blocks are equally configurable in the editor (Width, Width on mobile, Padding) and a
  # page composing either one reaches for the same settings.
  assign layout_classes = 'mionas-contact-form'

  # The field ids are derived here rather than inline at the render call: the render tag does not
  # accept filters on its arguments. The prefilled VALUES cannot be derived here -- they read the
  # `form` object, which only exists inside the form tag below.
  assign first_name_field_id = form_id | append: '-first-name'
  assign last_name_field_id = form_id | append: '-last-name'
  assign email_field_id = form_id | append: '-email'
  assign request_type_field_id = form_id | append: '-request-type'
  assign body_field_id = form_id | append: '-body'
%}

<div
  class="{{ layout_classes }} spacing-style"
  style="
    {%- render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings -%}
    {%- if block_settings.width == 'custom' -%}
      --mionas-contact-form-width: {{ block_settings.custom_width }}%;
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if block_settings.width_mobile == 'custom' -%}
      --mionas-contact-form-width-mobile: {{ block_settings.custom_width_mobile }}%;
    {%- endif -%}
  "
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- form 'contact', id: form_id -%}
    <input name="contact[id]" type="hidden" value="{{ form_id }}">

    {% liquid
      assign form_matches = false
      if form.id == form_id or form.id == blank
        assign form_matches = true
      endif

      # Shopify only ever reports an error against email on the contact form. Routed into the
      # field's own `error` param rather than a banner above the form, so the underline, the label
      # colour and the message all come from FormField/FormLabel/FormError as the design system
      # composes them.
      # Kept on one line: inside a liquid tag every newline ends the statement, so a filter
      # chain wrapped across lines is a syntax error, not a continuation.
      assign email_error = ''
      if form.errors and form_matches
        assign email_error = form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize | append: ' ' | append: form.errors.messages.email
      endif

      # Prefills, assigned here rather than in the block's opening liquid tag: the `form` object is
      # scoped to the form tag, so reading form.email outside it yields nothing and the field
      # silently comes back empty after a failed submit -- exactly when the user least wants to
      # retype it.
      #
      # form.name/form.first_name/form.last_name are deliberately NOT used here: Shopify's generic
      # form-object docs list only body/email/errors/id/posted_successfully? for a contact form --
      # no name, first_name or last_name -- so neither field repopulates after a failed submit for
      # any visitor, logged in or not. customer.first_name/customer.last_name (the real Customer
      # object properties, not form echoes) are used purely as the logged-in-customer default,
      # same role customer.email already played below.
      #
      # Tag names are spelled out in prose in these comments on purpose: a literal percent-brace
      # sequence inside a `#` comment line is still parsed as a tag, and naming a block tag that way
      # opens one the parser then never sees closed.
      assign first_name_value = customer.first_name
      assign last_name_value = customer.last_name
      assign email_value = form.email | default: customer.email
    %}

    {%- if form.posted_successfully? and form_matches -%}
      <div class="mionas-contact-form__success" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
        {{- 'icon-checkmark.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        {{ block_settings.success_text }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- capture contact_form_fields -%}
      {%- render 'mionas-text-field',
        label: block_settings.label_name,
        name: 'contact[first_name]',
        id: first_name_field_id,
        value: first_name_value,
        autocomplete: 'given-name',
        required: false,
        optional_text: block_settings.optional_text
      -%}

      {%- if block_settings.label_last_name != blank -%}
        {%- render 'mionas-text-field',
          label: block_settings.label_last_name,
          name: 'contact[last_name]',
          id: last_name_field_id,
          value: last_name_value,
          autocomplete: 'family-name',
          required: false,
          optional_text: block_settings.optional_text
        -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- render 'mionas-text-field',
        label: block_settings.label_email,
        name: 'contact[email]',
        id: email_field_id,
        type: 'email',
        value: email_value,
        placeholder: block_settings.placeholder_email,
        autocomplete: 'email',
        spellcheck: 'false',
        autocapitalize: 'off',
        error: email_error
      -%}

      {%- if block_settings.label_subject != blank -%}
        {%- capture subject_control -%}
          <select
            class="mionas-text-field__input mionas-contact-form__subject-select"
            id="{{ request_type_field_id }}"
            name="contact[request_type]"
          >
            <option value="">{{ block_settings.subject_placeholder }}</option>
            <option value="{{ block_settings.subject_option_1 | escape }}">{{ block_settings.subject_option_1 | escape }}</option>
            <option value="{{ block_settings.subject_option_2 | escape }}">{{ block_settings.subject_option_2 | escape }}</option>
            <option value="{{ block_settings.subject_option_3 | escape }}">{{ block_settings.subject_option_3 | escape }}</option>
            <option value="{{ block_settings.subject_option_4 | escape }}">{{ block_settings.subject_option_4 | escape }}</option>
          </select>
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- render 'mionas-form-field',
          control: subject_control,
          label: block_settings.label_subject,
          for: request_type_field_id,
          required: false,
          optional_text: block_settings.optional_text
        -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- render 'mionas-text-field',
        label: block_settings.label_message,
        name: 'contact[body]',
        id: body_field_id,
        value: form.body,
        placeholder: block_settings.placeholder_message,
        rows: 5,
        required: false,
        optional_text: block_settings.optional_text
      -%}

      {%- render 'mionas-submit-button',
        label: block_settings.submit_label,
        variant: block_settings.submit_variant,
        note: block_settings.note
      -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- liquid
      # The render tag does not accept filters on its arguments -- see the field-id comment above --
      # so the px suffix has to be applied here first.
      assign field_gap_css = block_settings.field_gap | append: 'px'
    -%}
    {%- render 'mionas-form', content: contact_form_fields, validate: true, gap: field_gap_css -%}
  {%- endform -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* No surface of its own -- see the file header comment. flex: 1 1 auto with width: 100% keeps the
     block from collapsing when a parent section stacks to a column on mobile; the desktop override
     zeroes flex-basis so a row splits by the sibling widths instead of by this 100%. Check
     mionas-form.liquid and mionas-email-signup.liquid when tuning this -- all three carry the same
     pattern. */
  .mionas-contact-form {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    width: var(--mionas-contact-form-width, 100%);
    font-family: var(--font-family-archivo);
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .mionas-contact-form {
      width: var(--mionas-contact-form-width-mobile, var(--mionas-contact-form-width, 100%));
    }
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .mionas-contact-form {
      flex-basis: 0;
    }
  }

  /* .mionas-text-field__input sets appearance: none, which strips the native chevron this select
     needs to read as a dropdown rather than plain text. Scoped here, not in that shared class,
     since only this one control needs it. */
  .mionas-contact-form__subject-select {
    appearance: auto;
  }

  /* No error banner counterpart: field-level errors are FormError's job, rendered by the field
     snippet. This is only the success confirmation, which the design system has no component for. */
  .mionas-contact-form__success {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Contact form",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_name",
      "label": "Name label",
      "default": "Nombre"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_last_name",
      "label": "Last name label",
      "default": "Apellidos"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_email",
      "label": "Email label",
      "default": "Email"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placeholder_email",
      "label": "Email placeholder",
      "default": "tu@email.com"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_subject",
      "label": "Subject label",
      "default": "Asunto"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subject_placeholder",
      "label": "Subject placeholder",
      "default": "Elige un tema…"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subject_option_1",
      "label": "Subject option 1",
      "default": "Un pedido"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subject_option_2",
      "label": "Subject option 2",
      "default": "Tarta por encargo"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subject_option_3",
      "label": "Subject option 3",
      "default": "Empresas y eventos"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subject_option_4",
      "label": "Subject option 4",
      "default": "Otro"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_message",
      "label": "Message label",
      "default": "Mensaje"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placeholder_message",
      "label": "Message placeholder",
      "default": "¿En qué te ayudamos?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "optional_text",
      "label": "Word shown after an optional field's label",
      "info": "Only email is required, so the name and message labels are suffixed with this in parentheses.",
      "default": "opcional"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "field_gap",
      "label": "Gap between fields",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24,
      "info": "24px matches the design system's own Form spacing (--space-lg)."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "submit_variant",
      "label": "Submit button style",
      "options": [
        { "value": "primary", "label": "Primary (filled)" },
        { "value": "outline", "label": "Outline" }
      ],
      "default": "primary"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "submit_label",
      "label": "Submit label",
      "default": "Enviar"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "Note below the button",
      "default": "Respuesta en 24–48h laborables"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "success_text",
      "label": "Success message",
      "default": "¡Mensaje enviado! Te respondemos en 24–48h laborables."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "width",
      "label": "Width",
      "options": [
        { "value": "fill", "label": "Fill available space" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "Custom" }
      ],
      "default": "fill",
      "info": "Fill lets the block share a row with its siblings and split the space between them. A custom width overrides that."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "custom_width",
      "label": "Width",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.width == 'custom' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "width_mobile",
      "label": "Width on mobile",
      "options": [
        { "value": "fill", "label": "Fill available space" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "Custom" }
      ],
      "default": "fill"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "custom_width_mobile",
      "label": "Width on mobile",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.width_mobile == 'custom' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "Left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "Right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Contact form",
      "category": "t:categories.forms"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
